SUMMARY:Draconid Meteor Shower: the one that happens at bedtime
DESCRIPTION:Nearly every meteor shower asks you to be awake at three in th
 e morning. The Draconids do not: the radiant is highest as the sky goes d
 ark\, so the best hour is the one right after dinner. The moon is a four 
 percent crescent that does not rise until quarter to five\, which means t
 he sky is as black as it gets all month.\nPrice: Free\nArea: Pensacola Be
 ach & Perdido\nTimes: Thu 10/08/2026 · from dark\, best in the first hou
 rs\nChecked against the venue's own page on 2026-09-11\nhttps://coastalev
 entures.com/events/ev-draconids-1008.html
